## Third-party acknowledgment

This software (the browser UI, the FastAPI bridge server, and the `.docx`
rendering pipeline in `frontend/` and `server/`) is original work covered by
the license above.

At runtime, it depends on a small part of a separate project:
**[ai-job-search](https://github.com/MadsLorentzen/ai-job-search)** by
**Mads Lorentzen**, itself MIT licensed. That project's `job-application-assistant`
skill supplies the actual job-fit scoring, gap-analysis, resume-tailoring, and
cover-letter logic this app calls into via the Claude Agent SDK — none of that
logic is reimplemented here.

Only the specific skill files this app's own code actually reads are included
directly in this repository, under
`backend/.claude/skills/job-application-assistant/` — see the `NOTICE.md` in
that folder for the exact file list and attribution, under his project's MIT
license. The rest of that project (its job-search/scraping tools, LaTeX/PDF
document generation, and interview-prep feature) is deliberately **not**
included, because JobLander doesn't use any of it.
